    "body": "Source inspection on upstream/main cda3d589 found a camera limitation, not a mill envelope used for a lathe.\n\ncrates/post/src/machine/envelope.rs selects a cylinder for Kind::Lathe. Z travel sets its ends. The largest absolute X limit sets its radius.\n\ncrates/ui/src/work_envelope.rs draws that cylinder around world Z. The turning paths also use world Z as the spindle axis.\n\nCamera::basis_right in crates/ui/src/viewport.rs always returns a vector with zero Z. Thus world Z has no horizontal screen component. Camera yaw and pitch cannot put the spindle axis horizontally on the screen.\n\nRotating only the envelope would separate it from the stock and turning paths. A consistent horizontal lathe view needs camera orientation support. Projection, picking, pan, orbit, and the view cube must agree on that orientation.\n\nThe travel check does not use the display cylinder. crates/app/src/machine/lathe_stroke.rs reads radial X and axial Z from the posted path. Source inspection found no wrong-frame travel check for this report. No safety code changed.\n\nRelated open PRs: #1689 changes Camera::eye and Camera::mvp. PR #2000 changes State::reset_for_open. Check these functions again before implementation.\n\nEscalated effort:medium to effort:high. The fix needs shared camera behavior and interaction tests, beyond the proposed envelope drawing change. No claim, branch, code change, or test run exists for this attempt. The issue remains free.\n",
    "author_association": "COLLABORATOR",
