    "body": "fix on issue/1993-lathe-envelope-axis · PR #2023 · pinned by a_lathe_lays_the_envelope_along_the_spindle_axis_left_to_right, a_mill_again_takes_the_milling_view_back, the_lathe_frame_keeps_pick_pan_and_the_view_cube_on_one_basis · merges when reviewed\n\nCause: `Camera::basis_right` in `crates/ui/src/viewport.rs` always crossed the view with world +Z. Thus world Z (the spindle axis of the envelope cylinder and of the turning paths) could not lie across the screen. The envelope data was correct.\n\nFix: the camera orbits in a view frame (`crates/ui/src/view_frame.rs`) that the machine kind selects. On a lathe, world +Z goes to the right and world +X goes up. This is a display change only. The world, the WCS, the toolpaths and the posted G-code do not change.\n\nTravel check: `crates/app/src/machine/lathe_stroke.rs` reads radial X and axial Z from the posted path. It does not use the display cylinder. No check used the wrong frame. The PR changes no safety code.",
